INT. GRAND HOTEL PARLOUR, SARATOGA - 1893 - AFTERNOON

A tea table laid for three. Gilded mirrors. A potted fern quivers in a draught from the verandah doors.

MRS. CORNELIA VANDERHOOF-ADEBAYO, 50s, rigid in black silk, presides over the pot. Her niece MISS BEATRIX ONWUACHI-LAW, 20s, in lavender, pleats a napkin. Across from them sits MADAME SOLANGE TREMBLAY-OKORO, 40s, a visitor, gloved and veiled, smiling thinly.

CORNELIA
Sugar, Madame?

SOLANGE
One lump.

CORNELIA
Beatrix, the tongs.

BEATRIX
Yes, Aunt.

CORNELIA
She never listens. You will find that of the young.

SOLANGE
I find it of the old as well.

CORNELIA
I beg your pardon?

SOLANGE
Nothing at all. The tea is excellent.

CORNELIA
It is from Ceylon.

SOLANGE
I should never have guessed. I took it for Darjeeling.

BEATRIX
Aunt prides herself on knowing the difference.

CORNELIA
Beatrix.

BEATRIX
Only as an observation.

SOLANGE
Observation is a great virtue, Miss Onwuachi-Law. Tell me, what do you observe about this room?

BEATRIX
The mirrors are very bright.

SOLANGE
And?

BEATRIX
The draught is not from the verandah.

CORNELIA
Beatrix, do not be absurd.

BEATRIX
It is from behind the fern.

SOLANGE
(setting down her cup)
I find your niece quite remarkable.

CORNELIA
She finds herself so.

SOLANGE
Mrs. Vanderhoof-Adebayo, when your husband died so suddenly in the spring, the physician said it was his heart.

CORNELIA
It was.

SOLANGE
And yet, the family lawyer tells me the will has been altered.

CORNELIA
Naturally. Estates are tidied.

SOLANGE
Altered in your favour.

CORNELIA
Madame Tremblay-Okoro, I invited you for tea, not for an inquest.

SOLANGE
But it is a tea, is it not? And teas, in my experience, are where the truth is poured.

Beatrix drops the tongs. The silver clatters on the china. Nobody moves to retrieve them.

BEATRIX
Aunt?

CORNELIA
Be quiet, child.

SOLANGE
Let her speak. She has been waiting two seasons.

Cornelia lifts the teapot. Her hand is perfectly steady. She pours, and the stream falls straight and gold into the empty cup before her.

CORNELIA
You are very sure of yourself.

SOLANGE
I am Pinkerton's agent in New York.

Behind the fern, a floorboard creaks. The draught stops.
